  <h2>Sound natural: reduce <span class="ex">to</span>, but keep the pattern recoverable</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Infinitive-marker <span class="ex">to</span> is commonly weak /tə/ in connected U.S. speech: <span class="ex">decided tə APPLY</span>, <span class="ex">tried tə FINish</span>. It may be fully stressed /tu/ when contrasted: <span class="ex">I said TO call, not that I called.</span> The <span class="ex">-ing</span> ending is normally /ɪŋ/, without a separate /g/: <span class="ex">WORKing</span>, <span class="ex">CHECKing</span>.</p>
  <p>Stress normally highlights the new or contrastive idea, not one permanently fixed grammar word. In a meaning-changing pair, the lexical context and complement must remain clear enough to recover: <span class="ex">I STOPPED checking</span> versus <span class="ex">I stopped tə CHECK one alert</span>.</p>
  <section data-lesson-extension="Tutor-read weak infinitive to, prepositional to plus -ing, stop contrast, try contrast, and information-stress listening check">
    <details class="reveal-card">
      <summary>Open the tutor listening check</summary>
      <div class="reveal-body">
        <p><b>Tutor:</b> Read each item once naturally without showing the transcript. Read it again only after the learner commits to an answer.</p>
        <ol>
          <li><span class="ex">Maya deCIDed tə APply for the project role.</span></li>
          <li><span class="ex">She’s looking FORward tə HEARing from the team.</span></li>
          <li><span class="ex">She STOPPED checking messages after dinner.</span></li>
          <li><span class="ex">During lunch, she stopped tə CHECK one alert.</span></li>
          <li><span class="ex">She tried TURNing notifications off, then tried tə RESTART the phone.</span></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </details>
    <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You recovered weak infinitive to, prepositional to plus -ing, the two stop meanings, and the experiment-versus-effort contrast with try.">
      <h3>Listen for the complement and its viewpoint</h3>
      <div class="quiz-list">
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Decide selects a to-infinitive, even when to is weak /tə/." data-hint="The reduced sound occurs between decided and apply." data-fix="Decide selects a to-infinitive, even when to is weak /tə/."><p class="quiz-question">1. What pattern is recoverable in the first line?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Decide selects a to-infinitive, even when to is weak /tə/.">Decide selects a to-infinitive, even when to is weak /tə/.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Decide selects applying with no infinitive marker.">Decide selects applying with no infinitive marker.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The weak sound changes apply into a noun.">The weak sound changes apply into a noun.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="To is a preposition, so hearing uses -ing." data-hint="Look forward to can also be followed by the reply or it." data-fix="To is a preposition, so hearing uses -ing."><p class="quiz-question">2. Why does the second line contain <span class="ex">to hearing</span>?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="To is a preposition, so hearing uses -ing.">To is a preposition, so hearing uses -ing.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Every to must be followed by -ing.">Every to must be followed by -ing.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Hearing is the Past Simple form of hear.">Hearing is the Past Simple form of hear.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Maya ended the after-dinner checking activity." data-hint="The tutor reads stopped directly with checking, with no new purpose action." data-fix="Maya ended the after-dinner checking activity."><p class="quiz-question">3. What happened in the third line?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya ended the after-dinner checking activity.">Maya ended the after-dinner checking activity.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya paused dinner in order to begin checking.">Maya paused dinner in order to begin checking.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya forgot whether she had a phone.">Maya forgot whether she had a phone.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Maya paused lunch in order to check one alert." data-hint="The to-infinitive names the purpose of stopping another activity." data-fix="Maya paused lunch in order to check one alert."><p class="quiz-question">4. What happened in the fourth line?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya paused lunch in order to check one alert.">Maya paused lunch in order to check one alert.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya permanently ended all alert checking.">Maya permanently ended all alert checking.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya continued lunch without any interruption.">Maya continued lunch without any interruption.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Turning notifications off is an experiment; restarting is an attempted action." data-hint="Try + -ing tests a method; try + to-infinitive presents an effort." data-fix="Turning notifications off is an experiment; restarting is an attempted action."><p class="quiz-question">5. What contrast does the final line create?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Turning notifications off is an experiment; restarting is an attempted action.">Turning notifications off is an experiment; restarting is an attempted action.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Both forms prove that every action succeeded.">Both forms prove that every action succeeded.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Restarting happened years before the experiment.">Restarting happened years before the experiment.</button></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <details class="reveal-card">
      <summary>Reveal the listening evidence</summary>
      <div class="reveal-body">
        <ol>
          <li>Weak /tə/ still marks the to-infinitive selected by <span class="ex">decide</span>.</li>
          <li><span class="ex">Look forward to</span> ends in a preposition, so <span class="ex">hearing</span> uses <span class="ex">-ing</span>.</li>
          <li><span class="ex">Stopped checking</span> ends the named activity.</li>
          <li><span class="ex">Stopped to check</span> pauses lunch for the purpose of checking.</li>
          <li><span class="ex">Tried turning</span> presents an experiment; <span class="ex">tried to restart</span> presents an effort.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <h2>Read a project update without guessing the complement</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Bridgeway career lab progress note</h3>
    <p>Maya considered applying for an internal project role after talking with her coach. The coach encouraged her to build a short portfolio and suggested revising its opening paragraph.</p>
    <p>Maya tried rewriting the paragraph as a story, and that experiment made it clearer. She also tried to finish the entire portfolio by Wednesday, but a power outage prevented her from completing it.</p>
    <p>She remembered meeting the hiring manager at a workshop last spring. Before sending the portfolio on Thursday, she remembered to attach the promised one-page summary.</p>
    <p>During lunch, Maya stopped working to call her mentor. After the call, she went on to draft a realistic first-month plan.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="note-line"><span class="ex">Go on doing</span> means continue the same activity. <span class="ex">Go on to do</span> means move to a later, different activity. The progress note supplies both the earlier call and the later drafting stage.</p>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You recovered the coach’s suggestion, the experimental rewrite, the unsuccessful effort, and the remembered responsibility from the progress note.">
    <h3>Reading check: connect form to evidence</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The coach suggested revising the opening paragraph." data-hint="The first paragraph states the coach’s recommendation directly." data-fix="The coach suggested revising the opening paragraph."><p class="quiz-question">1. What specific revision did the coach propose?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The coach suggested revising the opening paragraph.">The coach suggested revising the opening paragraph.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The coach suggested deleting the entire portfolio.">The coach suggested deleting the entire portfolio.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The coach refused to discuss the opening.">The coach refused to discuss the opening.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Rewriting the opening as a story was a successful experiment." data-hint="The note says that this method made the paragraph clearer." data-fix="Rewriting the opening as a story was a successful experiment."><p class="quiz-question">2. What does <span class="ex">tried rewriting</span> describe?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Rewriting the opening as a story was a successful experiment.">Rewriting the opening as a story was a successful experiment.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya made no change to the paragraph.">Maya made no change to the paragraph.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The story prevented Maya from writing anything.">The story prevented Maya from writing anything.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Maya attempted to finish by Wednesday, but the outage prevented completion." data-hint="The second paragraph states both the effort and the reason it failed." data-fix="Maya attempted to finish by Wednesday, but the outage prevented completion."><p class="quiz-question">3. What does <span class="ex">tried to finish</span> communicate here?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya attempted to finish by Wednesday, but the outage prevented completion.">Maya attempted to finish by Wednesday, but the outage prevented completion.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya tested finishing as one successful technical method.">Maya tested finishing as one successful technical method.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya refused to begin the portfolio.">Maya refused to begin the portfolio.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="She attached the promised one-page summary before sending." data-hint="Remember to attach means Maya did not forget the required action." data-fix="She attached the promised one-page summary before sending."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which responsibility did Maya complete on Thursday?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She attached the promised one-page summary before sending.">She attached the promised one-page summary before sending.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She canceled the workshop from last spring.">She canceled the workshop from last spring.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She removed every file from the application.">She removed every file from the application.</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build two complete complement paths</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="maya decided to submit the application after checking every date" data-hint="Begin with Maya decided to submit, then add the application and the after + -ing time phrase." data-fix="Maya decided to submit the application after checking every date." data-success-message="Correct. Decide selects to submit, and the preposition after selects checking.">
    <h3>Build 1: first verb plus later preposition</h3><p class="tile-target">Report Maya’s careful submission decision.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="checking">checking</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="maya">Maya</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="application">application</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="every">every</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="submit">submit</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="after">after</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="date">date</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="to">to</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="decided">decided</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="the coach encouraged maya to practice before presenting" data-hint="Begin with The coach encouraged Maya to practice, then add before presenting." data-fix="The coach encouraged Maya to practice before presenting." data-success-message="Correct. Encourage takes object Maya plus to practice, and before takes presenting.">
    <h3>Build 2: object plus to-infinitive</h3><p class="tile-target">Report the coach’s preparation advice.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="presenting">presenting</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="encouraged">encouraged</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="coach">coach</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="practice">practice</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="maya">Maya</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="before">before</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="to">to</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">The</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair the complement path</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="to" data-hint="Suggest opens the -ing path in this sentence." data-fix="The coach suggested revising the opening." data-why="Use suggest + -ing for the proposed activity; do not insert an infinitive marker in this structure." data-success-message="Correct. Suggested revising retrieves the intended verb family.">
    <h3>Repair 1: retrieve the verb family</h3><p>Tap the unnecessary word before <span class="ex">revise</span>.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="coach">The coach</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="suggested">suggested</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="to">to</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="revise">revise the opening.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="hear" data-hint="In look forward to, to is a preposition." data-fix="I look forward to hearing from the team." data-why="Prepositional to takes an -ing complement, just as it can take the noun reply." data-success-message="Correct. Hearing follows the preposition in look forward to.">
    <h3>Repair 2: identify prepositional <span class="ex">to</span></h3><p>Tap the verb with the wrong shape.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="look">I look forward</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="to">to</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="hear">hear</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="team">from the team.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="to" data-hint="The sentence says the wasteful activity ended; it does not describe pausing another activity for that purpose." data-fix="The deadline was close, so Maya stopped wasting time." data-why="Stop + -ing ends the named activity. Stop to waste would mean pause something else in order to waste time." data-success-message="Correct. Stopped wasting matches the stated end of the activity.">
    <h3>Repair 3: match the intended meaning</h3><p>The deadline was close, and Maya ended the wasteful behavior. Tap the word that creates the wrong meaning.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="deadline">The deadline was close,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="maya">so Maya stopped</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="to">to</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="waste">waste time.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Use the patterns without exposing a real application</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to reveal a real employer, application, salary, contract, manager, coworker, client, performance review, schedule, family responsibility, health detail, or private career decision. Use Maya, the Bridgeway career lab, and the fictional portfolio. Real details are optional.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Plan:</b> State what Maya considered doing, decided to do, hopes to do, and must remember to do.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Methods:</b> Suggest one experiment with <span class="ex">try + -ing</span>, then describe one effort with <span class="ex">try + to-infinitive</span> and a stated result.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Change:</b> Contrast one activity Maya ended with one moment when she paused another activity for a purpose.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Coaching:</b> Use one object + to-infinitive pattern and one active <span class="ex">let</span> or <span class="ex">make</span> + bare verb pattern.</div>

  <h2>Final production and check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: give a 75–90 second fictional career-lab update</h3>
    <p>Use a supplied project-role card and report Maya’s options, decision, preparation, experiment, unsuccessful effort, remembered responsibility, and next action. Include at least three stored verb families, two preposition + <span class="ex">-ing</span> patterns, one object + to-infinitive, one bare infinitive after <span class="ex">let</span> or <span class="ex">make</span>, and two meaning-changing contrasts. End by recommending one next step with <span class="ex">suggest + -ing</span> or <span class="ex">suggest that + clause</span>.</p>
    <p><b>Evidence check:</b> Can the listener identify what selected every complement, recover the intended meaning of each contrast, and hear weak <span class="ex">to</span> and final <span class="ex">-ing</span> without losing the grammar?</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved an -ing family, recognized prepositional to, interpreted a purpose infinitive after stop, and preserved the bare verb after active let.">
    <h3>Final check: defend the path and meaning</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Maya avoids sending unfinished drafts." data-hint="Avoid selects an -ing complement." data-fix="Maya avoids sending unfinished drafts."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which sentence uses the frequent complement pattern after <span class="ex">avoid</span>?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya avoids sending unfinished drafts.">Maya avoids sending unfinished drafts.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya avoids to send unfinished drafts.">Maya avoids to send unfinished drafts.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya avoids send to unfinished drafts.">Maya avoids send to unfinished drafts.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Maya is committed to improving the portfolio." data-hint="Committed to ends in prepositional to, so use -ing." data-fix="Maya is committed to improving the portfolio."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which sentence correctly completes the expression <span class="ex">be committed to</span>?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya is committed to improving the portfolio.">Maya is committed to improving the portfolio.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya is committed to improve the portfolio.">Maya is committed to improve the portfolio.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya is committed improving to the portfolio.">Maya is committed improving to the portfolio.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Maya paused another activity in order to call her mentor." data-hint="Stop + to-infinitive gives the purpose for pausing an activity supplied by context." data-fix="Maya paused another activity in order to call her mentor."><p class="quiz-question">3. In <span class="ex">During lunch, Maya stopped to call her mentor</span>, what does the complement mean?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya paused another activity in order to call her mentor.">Maya paused another activity in order to call her mentor.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya permanently ended all calls with her mentor.">Maya permanently ended all calls with her mentor.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Maya remembered a call from last spring.">Maya remembered a call from last spring.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The facilitator let Maya ask a follow-up question." data-hint="Active let takes object Maya + bare verb ask." data-fix="The facilitator let Maya ask a follow-up question."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which active sentence uses the standard pattern after <span class="ex">let</span>?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The facilitator let Maya ask a follow-up question.">The facilitator let Maya ask a follow-up question.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The facilitator let Maya to ask a follow-up question.">The facilitator let Maya to ask a follow-up question.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The facilitator let asking Maya a follow-up question.">The facilitator let asking Maya a follow-up question.</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
