  <h2>Reflect: what opened the complement path?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the decision path</h3>
    <p>Complete these ideas aloud: <span class="ex">I store frequent verbs as...</span> <span class="ex">After a preposition, I...</span> <span class="ex">I know to is a preposition when...</span> <span class="ex">An object + to-infinitive names...</span> <span class="ex">After active let or make, I...</span> <span class="ex">With stop, remember, try, and regret, context tells me...</span></p>
    <p>Choose one meaning-changing pair and create two mini-contexts that force the two different interpretations. Then explain why a form-only sentence without that context would be a weak test item.</p>
